        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la passoire",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la passoire — \"the colander, the sieve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il met les pâtes dans la passoire. He puts the pasta in the colander."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informal: une mémoire comme une passoire — a memory like a sieve."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "passoire is built on passer \"to pass\", which is inherited from Vulgar Latin passāre, built on Latin passus \"a step\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
